0..77 Comment "// Definitions a Rust caller runs on its own values, and a Rust function they"
78..112 Comment "// call, admitted against its row."
113..115 Comment "//"
116..194 Comment "// The first direction: Rust holds the composed program and calls a definition"
195..273 Comment "// by name. The second: the `extern` block declares the Rust caller\'s `add` as"
274..351 Comment "// an operation of the interface `Boundary`, and `quadrupled` performs it. No"
352..427 Comment "// handler here answers it, so the run offers it to the Rust caller\'s host,"
428..507 Comment "// which calls its own `add`. The block names `add`\'s row, and its check admits"
508..583 Comment "// the declared types against the row under Rust\'s default layout. No value"
584..663 Comment "// crosses by layout yet: the runtime holds each argument and answer as itself."
664..666 Comment "//"
667..743 Comment "// The Rust test composes this source, names each definition and calls it on"
744..821 Comment "// values it builds, then reads the answer back. Each `runs` item below makes"
822..899 Comment "// the same call from gandr, so both sides state one answer. `quadrupled` has"
900..955 Comment "// none, since only the Rust caller answers `Boundary`."
956..958 Comment "//"
959..1036 Comment "// - see: #2901 — not implemented: values crossing by Rust\'s default layout"
1037..1112 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
1113..1191 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — `admitBlock`, which the block\'s"
1192..1207 Comment "//   check runs"
1208..1285 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the function row an"
1286..1319 Comment "//   `extern` is admitted against"
1321..1364 Comment "// `Row`, `Codes`, `Code` and `admitBlock`."
